      "stem": "In the C++17 code below, `is_passing` must return a truth value (`true` or `false`) indicating whether `score` is at least `50`:\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n\n/* TYPE */ is_passing(int score) {\n    return score >= 50;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    if (is_passing(72)) {\n        std::cout << \"pass\\n\";\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n```\nWhich built-in type should replace `/* TYPE */`?",
