      "topic_id": "OOP_T01_1",
      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T01_1_LO02",
      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "In C++17, `Timer` defines default member initializers (`= 30` and `= false`) for its `public` fields, so empty-brace initialization `Timer t1{};` uses those defaults. What is the exact output of the following C++17 program?\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n\nstruct Timer {\n    int seconds = 30;\n    bool running = false;\n};\n\nint main() {\n    Timer t1{};\n    Timer t2{45, true};\n    t1.running = true;\n    std::cout << t1.seconds << \" \" << t1.running << \" | \"\n              << t2.seconds << \" \" << t2.running << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "`0 1 | 45 1`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "`30 0 | 45 1`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "`45 1 | 45 1`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "`30 1 | 45 1`"
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "D",
      "answer_explanation": "In `Timer t1{};`, both members are omitted from the brace list, so C++17 aggregate initialization uses their default member initializers (`seconds = 30`, `running = false`). Next, `Timer t2{45, true};` explicitly initializes `t2` to `45` and `true` (`1`). Setting `t1.running = true;` updates `t1.running` to `1` without changing `t1.seconds` (`30`) or `t2`. Output: `30 1 | 45 1`.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "`0 1 | 45 1` wrongly assumes `{}` zero-initializes `t1.seconds` to `0` while ignoring the default member initializer `= 30`.",
        "B": "`30 0 | 45 1` overlooks the assignment `t1.running = true;` before printing.",
        "C": "`45 1 | 45 1` wrongly assumes initializing `t2{45, true}` also overwrites `t1.seconds`."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "easy",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "default_member_initializer_in_aggregate",
        "independent_object_state"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/aggregate_initialization#Explanation",
        "https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/data_members#Layout"
      ],
      "verification_method": "cpp17_compile_and_run",
