      "question_id": "Q_OOP_T02_2_07",
      "question_family_id": "QF_OOP_T02_2_F07",
      "concept_id": "OOP_C02",
      "topic_id": "OOP_T02_2",
      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T02_2_LO02",
      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "A function accepts `const Ticket& t` (a `const` reference parameter that forbids modifying `t`), and fails to compile on `t.is_valid()`:\n```cpp\nclass Ticket {\nprivate:\n    bool valid_ = true;\npublic:\n    bool is_valid() { return valid_; }\n    void cancel() { valid_ = false; }\n};\n\nbool check(const Ticket& t) {\n    return t.is_valid(); // Compile error here\n}\n```\nWhich change fixes `check(const Ticket& t)` while preserving read-only safety for `const` objects and still allowing non-`const` `Ticket` objects to call `is_valid()` and `cancel()`?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "Mark `cancel()` as `void cancel() const { valid_ = false; }`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "Change `is_valid()` to `bool is_valid() const { return valid_; }`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "Remove `bool is_valid()` and make `valid_` `const bool valid_ = true;`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "Pass `Ticket` into `check` as `Ticket& t` and mark `is_valid()` non-`const`."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "Inside `check(const Ticket& t)`, `t` is treated as a `const` object, so it can only call `const` member functions. Adding trailing `const` to `bool is_valid() const` lets both `const` and non-`const` `Ticket` objects call `is_valid()`, while `cancel()` remains non-`const` so non-`const` tickets can still be cancelled.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "Marking `cancel() const` fails to compile because `valid_ = false;` modifies a data member inside a `const` function, and it does not fix `is_valid()`.",
        "C": "Making `valid_` a `const` data member prevents `cancel()` from ever changing `valid_ = false;`, breaking cancellation.",
        "D": "Removing `const` from `check`'s parameter breaks callers passing `const Ticket` objects and removes read-only protection in `check`."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "medium",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "const_reference_requires_const_method",
        "const_method_on_nonconst_object"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://www.learncpp.com/cpp-tutorial/const-class-objects-and-const-member-functions/",
        "https://isocpp.github.io/CppCoreGuidelines/CppCoreGuidelines#con2-by-default-make-member-functions-const"
      ],
      "verification_method": "cpp17_compile_expected_error",
      "agent_check_status": "passed",
