      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T02_3_LO01",
      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "What is the exact output of the following C++17 program?\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n\nclass ProgressBar {\nprivate:\n    int percent_;\npublic:\n    ProgressBar() : percent_(0) {}\n    ProgressBar(int pct)\n        : percent_(pct < 0 ? 0 : (pct > 100 ? 100 : pct)) {}\n    int percent() const { return percent_; }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ProgressBar a;\n    ProgressBar b(-15);\n    ProgressBar c(120);\n    std::cout << a.percent() << \" \" << b.percent() << \" \" << c.percent() << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "`0 0 100`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "`0 -15 120`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "`100 0 100`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "`0 15 100`"
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "A",
      "answer_explanation": "`ProgressBar a;` calls the default constructor `ProgressBar()`, setting `percent_` to `0`. `ProgressBar b(-15);` calls `ProgressBar(int pct)`, which clamps `-15 < 0` to `0`. `ProgressBar c(120);` clamps `120 > 100` to `100`. Thus the program prints `0 0 100`.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "B": "`0 -15 120` ignores the validation ternary expression that enforces the `[0, 100]` invariant.",
        "C": "`100 0 100` wrongly assumes the default constructor `ProgressBar()` initializes `percent_` to `100` instead of `0`.",
        "D": "`0 15 100` wrongly assumes `-15` is negated to `+15` rather than clamped to `0`."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "easy",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "constructor_invariant_clamping"
      ],
