      "answer_explanation": "All non-static data members are initialized before the constructor body executes. A `const` data member (without a default member initializer) cannot be default-initialized and later assigned inside `{ serial_ = s; }`; it must be initialized directly in the member initializer list (`: serial_(s)`).",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "`const` data members follow the exact same initialization rules in both `class` and `struct`.",
        "B": "Having a `const` member function like `int serial() const` is normal and has no conflict with parameterized constructors.",
        "D": "C++ constructors must have no return type (not even `void`)."
      },
