      "question_id": "Q_OOP_T02_3_06",
      "question_family_id": "QF_OOP_T02_3_F06",
      "concept_id": "OOP_C02",
      "topic_id": "OOP_T02_3",
      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T02_3_LO02",
      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "What is the exact output of the following C++17 program?\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n\nclass Ticket {\nprivate:\n    const int id_;\n    int price_;\npublic:\n    Ticket(int id, int p)\n        : id_(id), price_(p > 0 ? p : 10) {}\n    void print() const {\n        std::cout << id_ << \":\" << price_;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    Ticket t1(7, -5);\n    Ticket t2(8, 25);\n    t1.print();\n    std::cout << \" \";\n    t2.print();\n    std::cout << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "`7:-5 8:25`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "`7:10 8:25`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "`10:10 8:25`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "`7:0 8:25`"
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "Members are initialized in declaration order (`id_`, then `price_`). For `t1(7, -5)`, `id_` is initialized to `7` and `price_` is initialized via `p > 0 ? p : 10` to `10` (since `-5 <= 0`). For `t2(8, 25)`, `id_` is `8` and `price_` is `25`. Output: `7:10 8:25`.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "`7:-5 8:25` overlooks the `p > 0 ? p : 10` guard in `price_(...)`, which replaces `-5` with `10`.",
        "C": "`10:10 8:25` wrongly applies the fallback `10` to `id_` as well as `price_`.",
        "D": "`7:0 8:25` wrongly assumes invalid negative prices clamp to `0` instead of the specified fallback `10`."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "easy",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "initializer_list_tracing",
        "const_member_initialization"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
