      "question_category": "misconception_analysis",
      "stem": "A student claims that `return;` inside the `if` block jumps straight out of `run`, skipping destructors for `outer` and `inner`. What does this C++17 program actually print?\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n\nclass Guard {\nprivate:\n    char name_;\npublic:\n    Guard(char name) : name_(name) { std::cout << '+' << name_; }\n    ~Guard() { std::cout << '-' << name_; }\n};\n\nvoid run(bool stop_early) {\n    Guard outer('O');\n    if (stop_early) {\n        Guard inner('I');\n        std::cout << 'X';\n        return;\n    }\n    std::cout << 'Y';\n}\n\nint main() {\n    run(true);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "`+O+IX` (both destructors are skipped because `return;` exits before the closing brace of `run`)"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "`+O+IX-O-I` (`outer` is destroyed before `inner` when returning early)"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "`+O+IX-I` (`inner` is destroyed when leaving the `if` block, but `outer` is skipped)"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "`+O+IX-I-O` (`inner` is destroyed first, followed by `outer` in reverse order of construction)"
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "D",
      "answer_explanation": "When `run(true)` executes `return;`, control leaves both the `if` block and `run`'s block. C++ automatically destroys all active automatic objects in reverse construction order: `inner` (`-I`), then `outer` (`-O`), producing `+O+IX-I-O`.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "Automatic objects are destroyed whenever their enclosing scope exits—including via `return`—not only when falling off the final `}`.",
        "B": "Reverse construction order still holds on `return`: `inner` was constructed after `outer`, so `inner` is destroyed before `outer`.",
        "C": "Leaving `run` via `return;` exits `run`'s outer block as well, so `outer`'s destructor also executes."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "medium",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "early_return_destruction",
        "lifo_destruction_order"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
