      "topic_id": "OOP_T03_1",
      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T03_1_LO02",
      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "Consider the following C++17 classes with explicit ownership rules stated in the comments:\n```cpp\nclass IntSlotOwner {\nprivate:\n    int* slot_; // Exclusively owns the allocated int\npublic:\n    IntSlotOwner(int v) : slot_(new int(v)) {}\n    ~IntSlotOwner() { delete slot_; }\n    const int* get() const { return slot_; }\n};\n\nclass IntSlotViewer {\nprivate:\n    const int* target_; // Non-owning observer; owner outlives viewer\npublic:\n    IntSlotViewer(const int* target) : target_(target) {}\n    int value() const { return target_ ? *target_ : 0; }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    IntSlotOwner owner(15);\n    IntSlotViewer viewer(owner.get());\n    return (viewer.value() == 15) ? 0 : 1;\n}\n```\nWhich object owns the dynamically allocated `int` and is responsible for deleting it?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "`viewer` owns the allocated int because it was instantiated after `owner` and reads the target integer value directly."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "Both `owner` and `viewer` share joint ownership of the int, meaning each destructor must issue a `delete` call."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "`owner` owns the int (`slot_`) and deletes it in `~IntSlotOwner()` when `owner` leaves `main()`'s scope at return."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "Neither object possesses ownership; `main()` is required to invoke `delete` on `owner.get()` before returning."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "C",
      "answer_explanation": "`IntSlotOwner` acquires the `int` with `new int(v)` in its constructor and releases it in `~IntSlotOwner()` when `owner` leaves scope. `IntSlotViewer` only holds a non-owning observer pointer.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "`viewer` merely borrows `const int*` without owning it; `IntSlotViewer` neither allocates nor frees `target_`.",
        "B": "`IntSlotViewer` is explicitly non-owning, and having two independent objects delete the same pointer would cause a double-delete error.",
        "D": "Calling `delete` in `main()` would leave `~IntSlotOwner()` deleting an already-freed pointer; RAII keeps cleanup inside `IntSlotOwner`'s destructor."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "easy",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "owner_vs_observer",
        "raii_cleanup"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/cpp/object-lifetime-and-resource-management-modern-cpp?view=msvc-170#object-lifetime-and-resource-management-raii",
        "https://isocpp.github.io/CppCoreGuidelines/CppCoreGuidelines#r3-a-raw-pointer-a-t-is-non-owning",
        "https://isocpp.github.io/CppCoreGuidelines/CppCoreGuidelines#c31-all-resources-acquired-by-a-class-must-be-released-by-the-classs-destructor"
      ],
      "verification_method": "source_cross_check_and_cpp17_compile",
