      "question_id": "Q_OOP_T03_1_07",
      "question_family_id": "QF_OOP_T03_1_F07",
      "concept_id": "OOP_C03",
      "topic_id": "OOP_T03_1",
      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T03_1_LO02",
      "question_category": "misconception_analysis",
      "stem": "In a logging module, `Session` owns a heap-allocated `Metrics` object and deletes it in `~Session()`. `AuditHelper` stores a non-owning pointer `Metrics* ref_` passed in by `Session`. A teammate proposes adding `~AuditHelper() { delete ref_; }` \"just to be safe because every class with a pointer member should delete it.\" Why is that proposal wrong?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "Standard C++ forbids defining any destructor within a class containing raw pointer members, causing a compilation failure."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "An object of type `AuditHelper` cannot execute its destructor until the enclosing `Session` instance has fully exited scope first."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "Deleting `ref_` in `~AuditHelper()` automatically updates `Session`'s internal pointer to `nullptr` without deallocating the underlying object."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "`AuditHelper` does not own `ref_`; deleting it destroys `Metrics` prematurely while `Session` still owns it, causing double deletion."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "D",
      "answer_explanation": "Syntax (`T*`) does not imply ownership. Because `Session` owns the `Metrics` object and already deletes it in `~Session()`, having a non-owning `AuditHelper` also `delete ref_` destroys the resource early and leaves `Session` to double-delete.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "C++ allows destructors in classes with pointer members (for example, owning classes do define destructors); the issue here is non-ownership.",
        "B": "Local objects in nested scopes can have `AuditHelper` destroyed while `Session` is still alive; destructors do not require the owner to exit first.",
        "C": "`delete ref_` frees the pointed-to `Metrics` object and does not modify `Session`'s pointer member."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "easy",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "non_owning_raw_pointer",
        "premature_delete_misconception"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
