      "question_family_id": "QF_OOP_T03_2_F01",
      "concept_id": "OOP_C03",
      "topic_id": "OOP_T03_2",
      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T03_2_LO01",
      "question_category": "concept_recognition",
      "stem": "Consider the four labeled lines in `main()` below:\n```cpp\nclass Item {\npublic:\n    int code;\n    Item(int c) : code(c) {}\n    Item(const Item& other) : code(other.code) {}\n    Item& operator=(const Item& other) {\n        code = other.code;\n        return *this;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    Item a(10);   // Line 1\n    Item b = a;   // Line 2\n    Item c(20);   // Line 3\n    c = a;        // Line 4\n    return (b.code == c.code) ? 0 : 1;\n}\n```\nWhich classification of Line 2 and Line 4 is accurate?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "Both Line 2 and Line 4 invoke `operator=` because the assignment operator token `=` is present in both source statements."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "Line 2 invokes copy assignment `operator=`, while Line 4 initializes a new object via the copy constructor."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "Line 2 performs copy-initialization (calling the copy constructor); Line 4 performs copy assignment (calling `operator=`)."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "Both Line 2 and Line 4 invoke the copy constructor because source object `a` appears on the right-hand side in both lines."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "C",
      "answer_explanation": "`Item b = a;` declares and initializes a new `Item` from `a`, which is copy-initialization and calls the copy constructor `Item(const Item&)`. `c = a;` assigns into the already-constructed object `c`, calling `operator=`.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "The `=` in a variable declaration (`Item b = a;`) is initialization syntax, not an assignment expression.",
        "B": "This reverses the two operations: Line 2 creates `b` (copy constructor) and Line 4 updates existing `c` (`operator=`).",
        "D": "Having `a` on the right-hand side does not make Line 4 an initialization; `c` was already constructed on Line 3."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "easy",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "initialization_vs_assignment",
        "copy_constructor_recognition"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/copy_constructor#Explanation",
        "https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/copy_assignment#Explanation",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/cpp/copy-constructors-and-copy-assignment-operators-cpp?view=msvc-170#copy-constructors-and-copy-assignment-operators-c"
      ],
      "verification_method": "source_cross_check_and_cpp17_compile",
      "agent_check_status": "passed",
