      "topic_id": "OOP_T03_2",
      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T03_2_LO01",
      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "What is the exact output of the following C++17 program?\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n\nclass Badge {\nprivate:\n    int id_;\npublic:\n    Badge(int id) : id_(id) { std::cout << \"C(\" << id_ << \") \"; }\n    Badge(const Badge& other) : id_(other.id_) { std::cout << \"CC(\" << id_ << \") \"; }\n    Badge& operator=(const Badge& other) {\n        id_ = other.id_;\n        std::cout << \"CA(\" << id_ << \")\";\n        return *this;\n    }\n};\n\nvoid show(Badge param) {\n    Badge copy(param);\n    copy = param;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    Badge b(9);\n    show(b);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "`C(9) CC(9) CC(9) CA(9)`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "`C(9) CA(9) CC(9) CA(9)`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "`C(9) CC(9) CA(9) CA(9)`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "`C(9) CC(9) CC(9)`"
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "A",
      "answer_explanation": "`Badge b(9);` constructs `b` (`C(9) `). Passing `b` by value to `show(Badge param)` copy-initializes `param` using the copy constructor (`CC(9) `). Inside `show`, `Badge copy(param);` direct-initializes `copy` using the copy constructor (`CC(9) `), and `copy = param;` invokes copy assignment (`CA(9)`).",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "B": "Passing `b` by value initializes the new parameter `param`, so it calls the copy constructor (`CC`), not copy assignment (`CA`).",
        "C": "`Badge copy(param);` creates a new variable `copy` via direct-initialization, calling the copy constructor (`CC`), not `operator=`.",
        "D": "`copy = param;` assigns to the existing object `copy`, so `operator=` (`CA(9)`) definitely runs."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "medium",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "pass_by_value_copy_ctor",
        "direct_init_vs_assign"
      ],
