      "question_id": "Q_OOP_T03_2_06",
      "question_family_id": "QF_OOP_T03_2_F06",
      "concept_id": "OOP_C03",
      "topic_id": "OOP_T03_2",
      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T03_2_LO02",
      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "What is the exact output of the following C++17 program?\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n\nstruct BoxPtr {\n    int* ptr; // Copies address memberwise under implicit copy\n};\n\nint main() {\n    int value = 10;\n    BoxPtr a{&value};\n    BoxPtr b = a;\n    *b.ptr = 42;\n    std::cout << (a.ptr == b.ptr) << \" \" << *a.ptr << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "`1 42`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "`0 10`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "`1 10`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "`0 42`"
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "A",
      "answer_explanation": "`BoxPtr b = a;` uses the implicitly-defined copy constructor, copying `a.ptr` (the address `&value`) into `b.ptr`. Thus `a.ptr == b.ptr` evaluates to `true` (`1`), and writing `*b.ptr = 42` modifies `value`, so `*a.ptr` prints `42`.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "B": "Assumes `b` allocates a separate `int` copy of `10`, which shallow memberwise copy does not do.",
        "C": "Correctly recognizes `a.ptr == b.ptr` (`1`), but overlooks that writing through `b.ptr` modifies the shared `value` read by `*a.ptr`.",
        "D": "A pointer comparison `a.ptr == b.ptr` cannot be `0` (`false`) when `b.ptr` is copied directly from `a.ptr`."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "easy",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "shallow_copy_address_aliasing"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/copy_constructor#Implicitly-defined_copy_constructor",
        "https://www.learncpp.com/cpp-tutorial/shallow-vs-deep-copying/"
      ],
      "verification_method": "cpp17_compile_and_run",
      "agent_check_status": "passed",
