      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T04_3_LO01",
      "question_category": "misconception_analysis",
      "stem": "A student declares `TimedTask` inheriting from `Task` and instantiates `TimedTask t;` below, expecting it to compile because `TimedTask` overrides `run()`:\n```cpp\nclass Task {\npublic:\n    virtual ~Task() = default;\n    virtual void run() = 0;\n    virtual int priority() const = 0;\n};\n\nclass TimedTask : public Task {\npublic:\n    void run() override {}\n};\n\nint main() {\n    TimedTask t;\n    t.run();\n    return 0;\n}\n```\nWhy does `TimedTask t;` fail to compile?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "Because `TimedTask` did not explicitly write `virtual` before `void run() override {}`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "Because `TimedTask` does not override `Task::priority()`, so `TimedTask` inherits an un-overridden pure virtual function and remains an abstract class."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "Because any class that inherits from an abstract base class can never be instantiated, even if it overrides all pure virtual methods."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "Because `Task` has a defaulted destructor `= default`, which prohibits derived classes from instantiating."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "A class is abstract if it defines **or inherits** at least one function whose final overrider is pure virtual. Because `TimedTask` overrides `run()` but does not override `priority()`, `Task::priority()` remains pure virtual in `TimedTask`, so `TimedTask` is still abstract and cannot be instantiated.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "Omitting `virtual` on an overriding function in a derived class is completely valid; the problem is the missing override of `priority()`.",
        "C": "A derived class becomes concrete and instantiable as soon as it provides non-pure overrides for all inherited pure virtual functions.",
        "D": "`virtual ~Task() = default;` is valid and does not make a derived class abstract."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "medium",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "partial_override_still_abstract"
      ],
