      "topic_id": "OOP_T05_1",
      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T05_1_LO01",
      "question_category": "concept_recognition",
      "stem": "In an online store design with explicit lifetime rules:\n1. Each `Order` exclusively owns its `LineItem` parts; `LineItem` objects are created with that `Order` and destroyed when that `Order` is destroyed.\n2. Each `Order` links to a `Customer` account that is created independently, outlives individual orders, and may be referenced by many `Order` objects at once.\nWhich classification accurately describes these two relationships?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "`Order`–`LineItem` is an association (`uses-a`), while `Order`–`Customer` is a composition (`owns-a`)."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "Both `Order`–`LineItem` and `Order`–`Customer` are compositions (`owns-a`) because `Order` interacts with both classes."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "`Order`–`LineItem` is a composition (`owns-a`) because `Order` exclusively owns and manages `LineItem` lifetimes, while `Order`–`Customer` is an association (`uses-a`) because `Customer` has an independent, shareable lifetime."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "Both `Order`–`LineItem` and `Order`–`Customer` are inheritance (`is-a`) relationships."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "C",
      "answer_explanation": "Composition (`owns-a`) holds when the whole exclusively owns its parts and manages their creation and destruction (`Order`–`LineItem`). Association (`uses-a`) holds when linked objects have independent lifetimes, neither destroys the other, and an object may be shared across multiple users (`Order`–`Customer`).",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "This reverses both relationships: `Order` manages `LineItem` lifetimes (composition), whereas `Customer` exists independently and is shared across orders (association).",
        "B": "Simply interacting with another class does not create composition; `Order` does not own or destroy `Customer`.",
        "D": "Inheritance models `is-a` specialization; an `Order` is neither a `LineItem` nor a `Customer`."
      },
