      "question_family_id": "QF_OOP_T05_1_F08",
      "concept_id": "OOP_C05",
      "topic_id": "OOP_T05_1",
      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T05_1_LO02",
      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "Read the following class diagram together with its supplied notation legend:\n```text\n+------------+  1  ◆-------- 1..* +--------+  0..*  assigned_to  0..* +-------+  0..*  uses  0..1 +-------+\n|  Hospital  |------------------->|  Ward  |<----------------------->| Nurse |------------------>| Pager |\n+------------+                    +--------+                         +-------+                   +-------+\n\nLegend:\n  ◆---  Composition (owner at diamond end manages lifetime of part)\n  <---> Bidirectional association (both ends navigate to each other; independent lifetimes)\n  --->  Unidirectional navigable association (only source navigates to target; independent lifetimes)\n  1, 0..1, 0..*, 1..*  Multiplicity at that role end (one, zero or one, zero or more, one or more)\n```\nBased strictly on this diagram and legend, which statement satisfies **all** relationship and multiplicity constraints?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "A `Hospital` can exist with zero `Ward`s, and destroying a `Ward` destroys every `Nurse` assigned to it."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "Each `Pager` navigates directly to its assigned `Nurse`, and each `Nurse` must carry at least one `Pager` at all times."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "Each `Hospital` owns `1..*` `Ward` parts and manages their lifetimes; `Ward` and `Nurse` have a bidirectional `0..*` association with independent lifetimes; and each `Nurse` can navigate to `0..1` `Pager` without owning it or giving `Pager` navigation back to `Nurse`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "Because `Ward` has `0..*` toward `Nurse`, a `Nurse` owns all `Ward`s she is assigned to."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "C",
      "answer_explanation": "Checking each connector against the legend: (1) `Hospital` has the filled diamond (`◆`) and `1`, while `Ward` has `1..*`, so `Hospital` owns one or more `Ward`s and manages their lifetimes; (2) `Ward <---> Nurse` has `0..*` at both ends and no diamond, giving a bidirectional many-to-many association with independent lifetimes; (3) `Nurse ---> Pager` is a unidirectional association with `0..1` at `Pager`, so a `Nurse` can locate zero or one `Pager` independently while `Pager` does not navigate back to `Nurse`.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "`Ward` has multiplicity `1..*` (so `Hospital` must own at least one `Ward`), and `Ward <---> Nurse` is an association (independent lifetimes, so destroying `Ward` does not destroy `Nurse`).",
        "B": "`Nurse ---> Pager` is unidirectional from `Nurse` to `Pager` (so `Pager` does not navigate back), and `0..1` allows a `Nurse` to have zero `Pager`s.",
        "D": "There is no composition diamond between `Ward` and `Nurse`, and `0..*` is a multiplicity rather than an ownership marker."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "medium",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "multiplicity_0_1_vs_1_plus",
        "bidirectional_vs_unidirectional_association",
        "uml_diamond_direction"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/visualstudio/visual-studio-2015/modeling/uml-class-diagrams-reference?view=vs-2015#reading-class-diagrams",
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/visualstudio/visual-studio-2015/modeling/properties-of-associations-on-uml-class-diagrams?view=vs-2015#properties-of-each-role"
      ],
