      "question_category": "misconception_analysis",
      "stem": "A student opens an existing file `\"notes.txt\"` containing `\"Line1\\nLine2\\n\"` using `std::ofstream out(\"notes.txt\");` and then executes `out << \"Line3\\n\";`, expecting the file to keep `Line1` and `Line2`. Why are `Line1` and `Line2` lost?",
