      "question_category": "concept_recognition",
      "stem": "Assume the temporary directory is available, no other process changes the chosen file, and all shown filesystem and stream operations succeed except the intentionally missing-file open (if any).\n\nIn the C++17 program below, the temporary file initially receives `\"12 34\\n\"`. What is the exact output printed to `std::cout`?\n```cpp\n#include <filesystem>\n#include <fstream>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n\nint main() {\n    std::filesystem::path p = std::filesystem::temp_directory_path() / \"oop_t06_1_q5.txt\";\n    {\n        std::ofstream init(p);\n        init << \"12 34\\n\";\n    }\n    {\n        std::ofstream rewrite(p, std::ios::out | std::ios::trunc);\n        rewrite << \"56\\n\";\n    }\n    std::ifstream in(p);\n    std::string line;\n    std::getline(in, line);\n    std::cout << line << \"\\n\";\n    in.close();\n    std::filesystem::remove(p);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
