      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "Assume the temporary directory exists, the chosen file is not shared, and all shown file operations succeed except reads that reach the end of the supplied data. The setup creates the exact text shown.\nEach complete record requires two integers: id and points. The final `2` has no points value. What output line is printed?\n```cpp\n#include <filesystem>\n#include <fstream>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n\nint main() {\n    auto p = std::filesystem::temp_directory_path() / \"oop_b05_partial.txt\";\n    { std::ofstream seed(p); seed << \"1 10\\n2\"; }\n    std::ifstream in(p);\n    int id = 0, points = 0, count = 0, total = 0;\n    while (in >> id >> points) { ++count; total += points; }\n    std::cout << count << \" \" << total << \"\\n\";\n    in.close();\n    std::filesystem::remove(p);\n}\n```",
