      "learning_objective_id": "OOP_T07_1_LO01",
      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "For these `int` and `double` calls, `<` compares the values and `condition ? yes : no` selects `yes` when the condition is true. What output line does this C++17 program print?\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\ntemplate<typename T> T smaller(T a, T b) { return b < a ? b : a; }\nint main() { std::cout << smaller(9, 4) << \" \" << smaller(1.5, 2.5) << \"\\n\"; }\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "`9 2.5`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "`4 1.5`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "`4 2.5`"
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "`9 1.5`"
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "For `9` and `4` the condition `4 < 9` is true, so the `int` call returns `4`. For `1.5` and `2.5` the condition `2.5 < 1.5` is false, so the `double` call returns `1.5`.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "Students who read `b < a ? b : a` backwards return the larger argument in both calls, whereas true selects `b` (`4`) and false selects `a` (`1.5`).",
        "C": "Some learners pick the second argument for both calls, yet `2.5 < 1.5` is false so the `double` instantiation returns its first parameter, `1.5`.",
        "D": "A student might return the first argument in both calls, missing that `4 < 9` is true so the `int` instantiation returns `b`, which is `4`."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "easy",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "ternary_branch_reversal",
        "template_type_instantiation",
        "floating_point_preservation"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/cpp/function-templates?view=msvc-170"
      ],
      "verification_method": "cpp17_compile_and_run",
      "agent_check_status": "awaiting_independent_review",
      "human_review_status": "pending",
      "approved_by": null,
