        "B": "Learners sometimes apply the operation only to the `int` call, missing that `square<double>(2.5)` instantiates its own `double` function returning `6.25`.",
        "D": "Some students square `2` and `0.5` separately to get `4.25`, whereas `square<double>(2.5)` evaluates the full product `2.5 * 2.5 = 6.25`."
