      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "In the C++17 program below, `ARG` stands for one of the expressions in the options.\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n\ntemplate <class T>\nstruct Box {\n    T value;\n};\n\nint unwrap(Box<int> b) {\n    return b.value + 1;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::cout << unwrap(ARG) << \"\\n\";\n}\n```\nWhich expression, used in place of `ARG`, makes the program compile and print `5`?",
