      "question_category": "misconception_analysis",
      "stem": "`Token` has copy construction but no `operator+`. Consider the C++17 program below.\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n\ntemplate <class T>\nstruct Adder {\n    T add(T a, T b) { return a + b; }\n};\n\nstruct Token {\n    int id;\n};\n\nint main() {\n    Adder<int> ints;\n    Adder<Token> tokens;\n    std::cout << ints.add(2, 3) << \"\\n\";\n    Token t = tokens.add(Token{1}, Token{2});\n    std::cout << t.id << \"\\n\";\n}\n```\nWhat happens when this program is compiled?",
