      "question_category": "misconception_analysis",
      "stem": "In the C++17 code below, `fetch_record()` may throw `int` before `process()` returns:\n```cpp\nstruct Handle {\n    void release() { /* closes handle */ }\n};\n\nvoid process() {\n    Handle h;\n    fetch_record(); // may throw int\n    h.release();\n}\n```\nIf `fetch_record()` throws, `h.release()` is skipped. Which change guarantees cleanup during unwinding?",
