      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "Trace the C++17 program below, in which two screens obtain a shared `ScreenCache`:\n```cpp\n#include <iostream>\n\nclass ScreenCache {\nprivate:\n    int theme_id_ = 1;\n    ScreenCache() = default;\npublic:\n    ScreenCache(const ScreenCache&) = delete;\n    ScreenCache& operator=(const ScreenCache&) = delete;\n    static ScreenCache& instance() {\n        static ScreenCache cache;\n        return cache;\n    }\n    void set_theme(int id) { theme_id_ = id; }\n    int theme() const { return theme_id_; }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ScreenCache& profile_view = ScreenCache::instance();\n    ScreenCache& home_view = ScreenCache::instance();\n    profile_view.set_theme(3);\n    std::cout << home_view.theme() << \"\\n\";\n}\n```\nA design review asks whether `profile_view` changing the cache can affect `home_view`. What does the program print and why?",
