      "question_category": "short_application",
      "stem": "C# 5: a class assignment copies a reference; a struct assignment copies its contained values. Both types below contain only an int. After these fragments, what values are read from `a.N` and `s.N`?\n```csharp\nclass C { public int N; }\nstruct S { public int N; }\n// Inside Main():\nC a = new C(); a.N = 1; C b = a; b.N = 5;\nS s = new S(); s.N = 1; S t = s; t.N = 5;\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "a.N = 1; s.N = 1."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "a.N = 5; s.N = 5."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "a.N = 5; s.N = 1."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "a.N = 1; s.N = 5."
        }
      ],
