      "title_en": "Class & Object Modeling Lab: Independent Object State and Procedural Comparison",
      "title_vi": "Thực hành Lớp & Đối tượng: Trạng thái độc lập và So sánh mô hình thủ tục",
      "activity_type": "cpp_coding",
      "problem_statement": "Model a small `WaterTank` type that groups state (`int capacity_ml`, `int level_ml`) with behavior (`int fill(int amount_ml)`, `int drain(int amount_ml)`) without using custom constructors, inheritance, or templates.\n1. `fill(int amount_ml)` adds up to `capacity_ml - level_ml` (ignoring non-positive amounts) and returns the actual milliliters added.\n2. `drain(int amount_ml)` removes up to `level_ml` (ignoring non-positive amounts) and returns the actual milliliters drained.\n3. Also implement a procedural equivalent `int proc_fill(int capacity_ml, int& level_ml, int amount_ml)` operating on separate variables so you can verify identical numeric results while observing how the object model bundles `capacity_ml` and `level_ml` inside each `WaterTank` instance.\nCreate two explicitly aggregate-initialized instances `tankA{500, 100}` and `tankB{300, 250}` and assert that mutating `tankA` does not alter `tankB`.",
      "input_spec": "Two aggregate-initialized `WaterTank{capacity_ml, level_ml}` instances and non-negative/negative `int` amounts.",
      "output_spec": "`fill` and `drain` mutate only the target instance and return actual volume transferred; `main()` verifies instance independence and procedural equivalence, printing `ACT_OOP_LAB_02_PASS:<A>,<B>`.",
      "constraints": "C++17 (`g++ -std=c++17 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror`); do not use inheritance, templates, virtual methods, or custom constructors (aggregate initialization `{cap, lvl}` keeps scope strictly in C01).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "input": "WaterTank a{500, 100}; WaterTank b{300, 250}; a.fill(600); b.drain(100);",
          "output": "a.fill returns 400 (a.level_ml == 500), b.drain returns 100 (b.level_ml == 150)"
        }
      ],
      "rubric_and_test_cases": [
        {
          "test_id": "TC1",
          "description": "Two instances maintain independent state",
          "expected": "Mutating tankA leaves tankB.level_ml and tankB.capacity_ml unchanged"
        },
        {
          "test_id": "TC2",
          "description": "Clamping on fill and drain plus non-positive input guard",
          "expected": "fill/drain return 0 for <=0 and clamp within [0, capacity_ml]"
        },
        {
          "test_id": "TC3",
          "description": "Procedural vs object-oriented comparison",
          "expected": "proc_fill on standalone variables matches WaterTank::fill behavior"
        }
      ],
      "reference_solution_cpp": "#include <cassert>\n#include <iostream>\n\nstruct WaterTank {\n    int capacity_ml;\n    int level_ml;\n\n    int fill(int amount_ml) {\n        if (amount_ml <= 0 || level_ml >= capacity_ml) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        int space = capacity_ml - level_ml;\n        int added = amount_ml < space ? amount_ml : space;\n        level_ml += added;\n        return added;\n    }\n\n    int drain(int amount_ml) {\n        if (amount_ml <= 0 || level_ml <= 0) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        int removed = amount_ml < level_ml ? amount_ml : level_ml;\n        level_ml -= removed;\n        return removed;\n    }\n};\n\nint proc_fill(int capacity_ml, int& level_ml, int amount_ml) {\n    if (amount_ml <= 0 || level_ml >= capacity_ml) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n    int space = capacity_ml - level_ml;\n    int added = amount_ml < space ? amount_ml : space;\n    level_ml += added;\n    return added;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    WaterTank tankA{500, 100};\n    WaterTank tankB{300, 250};\n\n    int addedA = tankA.fill(600);\n    assert(addedA == 400 && tankA.level_ml == 500);\n    assert(tankB.level_ml == 250 && tankB.capacity_ml == 300);\n\n    int drainedB = tankB.drain(100);\n    assert(drainedB == 100 && tankB.level_ml == 150);\n    assert(tankA.fill(-10) == 0 && tankB.drain(0) == 0);\n\n    int proc_cap = 500;\n    int proc_lvl = 100;\n    assert(proc_fill(proc_cap, proc_lvl, 600) == 400 && proc_lvl == 500);\n\n    std::cout << \"ACT_OOP_LAB_02_PASS:\" << tankA.level_ml << \",\" << tankB.level_ml << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "expected_stdout": "ACT_OOP_LAB_02_PASS:500,150",
